2586-- Alex, to the three choices on the review page (`docs/research/2026-10-27-pipeline-review/index.html`, main branch): "我都同意但一样你的黄金标准要有然后自己下去改和量化测试，先小范围验证可行，深度解读错误的trace不要乱做test和乱改一定要知道问根因".
2587-- Decided: (1) Jev's output is an opinion with a score (same statement / revision / different; direct result / business lead / background / unrelated / uncertain); whether a source is kept, merged or placed is decided by the analysis step that reads the complete old and new content. (2) The library keeps both the source records (immutable, for tracing) and the research argument each question carries, updated as a new version with what changed, its supporting and opposing sources, whether they are independent, and its limitations; the judgement reads the argument and its sources, not only the flat evidence list. (3) A new question opens only on an independent investment judgement with the full admission contract; a new product, a new figure or a narrower scope alone does not open one.
2588-- Method, Alex's: a written gold before the first send (reference answers for every case, held-out cases included), one small scope (about 20 incoming records at their historical library state) measured against a fresh control of the current path, quantified per case; a failure is traced to its raw answer and its mechanism before any test or change; no tuning on the cases that were read.
2589-- This decision changes the thesis-library PRD (06-views: the argument record and its writer/reader) and the matching PRD (Jev as opinion); the PRD text follows the measured build, not before it. No production change and no paid call in this decision itself.
--
2960-  2. **One event, several deadlines** (H2, "A"): while the earlier-deadline question is open, a later deadline is its evidence, not a new question; when the earlier one falls due unresolved and the matter is still live, the system opens the next-deadline successor with the merged evidence, without waiting for a new article (new work for pull mode, D14, D54).
2961-  3. **One product generation, several milestones** (H3, "A"): one question per generation, asked at the step that brings revenue (shipments begin); sampling and launch are its evidence; only milestones an analyst bets on separately (a drug's phase-3 data and its approval) are separate questions.
2962-  4. **A company's own quantity by fiscal and by calendar year** (H4, "A"): only the fiscal year opens (PRD 06 ladder rule 5); a calendar-year estimate is evidence to the fiscal question, weighed lower when the years differ much.
2963-  5. **A model-written period start** (H5, "A"): for event and policy questions it no longer blocks a merge; object, event and due day are still checked.
2964-  6. **Small matters opened as questions** (H6, "A， A"): a deal, product or project (the question was put about small deals and products) opens a question only when its scale can change the company's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk; otherwise no question opens, and whether its statement is kept follows the evidence rule (standard §5). Done in this round together with the merge changes, each measured as its own arm, then together on the holdout. Narrows the standard §3 class C ("a sized, not yet completed stake or acquisition").
2965-  7. **The same statement carried by several outlets** (H7, "A"): code treats pieces with the same known original speaker, original day and figures as one (an unknown speaker or day never matches: 297 of the sealed run's 4,298 pieces have both unknown); the judge sees it once with the outlet count; every piece is still stored. Changes D204's "both shown to the judge" for this case, and is a chosen exception to AGENTS §3 "equal values alone never establish identity"; the risk put to him with the question (a qualification such as "excluding China sales" hidden; D204's 8 of 40 wrong merges) is measured on the G3 gold before it is switched on, as is the accuracy of the original-speaker and original-day fields it relies on.
